{
  "slug": "skillcheck-free",
  "name": "Skillcheck Free",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "SkillCheck Free validates Claude Code SKILL.md files against ~25 contract rules covering structure, naming, semantic consistency, and quality patterns. It catches missing frontmatter, weak or ambiguous descriptions, trigger collisions, anti-pattern formatting (prose where tables belong), naming smells, and contradictions before users encounter them.\n\nRuns locally — it's itself a SKILL.md the agent reads, with no API calls, binaries, or external services. MIT-licensed. Works in Claude Code, Claude Desktop/Web (Projects), and Cursor.\n\nThe Free tier covers structural, semantic, and naming checks plus quality-pattern recognition. SkillCheck Pro (separate product at getskillcheck.com) adds anti-slop detection, security scanning, token budget analysis, WCAG accessibility, and enterprise readiness checks.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `skill-check` (Validate Claude Code skills against Anthropic guidelines).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install skillcheck-free@claude-community` from `olgasafonova/SkillCheck-Free`.\n\nValidate AI coding assistant skills against the agentskills specification. Works with Claude Code, Claude Desktop/Web, and Cursor. Catch issues before your users do.",
